From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Brian McKenna <brian@brianmckenna.org>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 12:24:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(shader): keep failed compiles in the disk cache

A resource plan build or variant emission that throws was remembered
only in memory, so every run compiled each failing stage again before
failing (a title with a few hundred such stages paid for all of them at
every start, and its plan misses stayed far above its plan writes).
The failure is now written under the entry's own key, with the same
format, source version, key and hash checks as a compiled entry, as its
error text and the code address it failed at; a later run rethrows it
at that address without compiling. APS5_NO_FAILURE_MEMO=1 neither stores
nor reads them. The cache counts their hits and writes apart from the
compiled entries'.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
